WEBVTT

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:14.410
I missed all but one of my conversion kicks
because you were nearby.

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:17.330
Wh-Wh-Wh-What do you mean?!

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:21.120
I haven't been doing well ever since
you became the team manager.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.750
Wh-Why?!

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:24.580
You didn't have a problem last year!

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:26.450
We both played on the same team!

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:28.330
I don't know.

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:31.370
Wait, what do you mean you don't know?

00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:34.120
Isn't there something?
Like the feeling that something is off?

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.040
Yes, there is.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:39.200
My body gets stiff when Natsu is watching me.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.160
I can't do it how I practiced.

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:45.370
Oh, Seiichirou. That's probably called
the feeling of nervousness.

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:46.700
Nervousness?

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:52.160
You know. The feeling of your body
tensing up strangely or your heart racing...

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:58.250
I feel tension around my stomach
when I get on a plane.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:00.330
Yeah, yeah. That's probably nervousness.

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:03.120
So, he gets nervous on planes?

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:04.410
B-B-B-But!

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:08.000
Doesn't that mean he's just blaming me
for his own weak mental state?!

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.410
I'm not blaming you. It's my own fault.

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:14.620
I was only stating the fact that
I can't score with you around.

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:18.000
Th-That's not the point!

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.160
Ibuki-<i>san</i>!

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:21.000
W-Will things be all right?

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.410
No, they won't.

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:27.120
Fights between those two are really long.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:31.700
Natsusa gets really emotional
when he fights with Seiichirou.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:38.410
On the other hand, Seiichirou responds so calmly
that it makes Natsusa more angry.

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:42.250
To begin with, those two aren't even
sure about the problem this time...

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:44.250
Then practice some more!

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:46.160
There are only two weeks left.

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:48.000
It's faster if you don't come.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.330
Then who'll do your taping?!

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:52.870
You can do the taping, then go home.

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:55.830
What?! I can't believe you can
even say something like that!

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:57.200
What a turn off!

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.700
Well, it's fine.

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:00.370
He was so depressed a second ago.

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:02.540
Now, Natsusa's super energetic.

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:04.870
No, no, no, no...

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:37.160
"The goal and method often
gets muddled in the process."

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:38.700
"The goal and method often
gets muddled in the process."
Forget it!

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:41.950
Okay...

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:47.870
Okay, my ass!

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:49.660
How many times do I have to tell you?!

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:54.750
It's the worse case scenario
if I say, "Forget it!" in this situation!

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:56.120
Forget it!

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:59.870
Liar. You don't really mean that.

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:01.950
It really doesn't matter anymore!

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:03.290
Look at me.

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:04.950
Leave me alone!

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:06.580
There's no way I can leave you alone.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:10.910
I taught you to do that kind of forceful
questioning at least three times!

00:04:10.910 --> 00:04:12.950
So troublesome!

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:15.910
That is a bit troublesome...

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:18.410
Okay! That's enough.

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:20.080
Let's go back home to Oita.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.450
I got tickets and booked a hotel.

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:25.120
The bullet train tonight.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:29.000
We'll go play around tomorrow
and head home Tuesday morning.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.750
What kind of nonsense...?

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:33.450
It's important to refresh yourself
every once in a while, you know.

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:38.580
Seiichirou's problem might get better
after getting good and rested, too.

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:42.290
But Taku-<i>senpai </i>is in the hospital...

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:45.750
It's not a good idea to visit Takumi
tomorrow and the day after.

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:48.830
His family will be visiting him
and Taisei will be by his side.

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:54.500
Taisei will be bothered by us...
Well, mainly by me...

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:56.000
But...

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:59.330
Yasunari and Yuu-<i>kun</i>
want to go, too, right? To Oita.

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:00.410
Huh?

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:05.290
I-I want to go!

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:07.120
Let's go, Natsusa-<i>san</i>!

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:08.120
Huh?

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:09.450
Please!

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:13.370
Uh, o-okay... I guess we can go?

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:19.700
Okay, lets pack and meet back here in two hours.

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:25.410
Is it really okay to accept this?!

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:26.950
Please. Please.

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:30.330
I'm not really good with it and was
wondering what do to with the thing.

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:33.250
The specs on this tablet are
better than the last one I had!

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:36.540
I'm so happy! Thank you very much!

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:38.000
Yasunari.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:38.910
Yes?

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:48.910
"Taking a look at the 108 earthly desires"

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:40.870
"Taking a look at the 108 earthly desires"
Take a look at this.

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:41.790
Take a look at this.

00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:44.290
What is this?

00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:47.750
Sasaki said this might be
the reason I get nervous.

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:50.830
Do any of these happen to you
when you play rugby?

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:55.160
Um, f-fixation maybe?

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:59.410
Wanting to win makes you nervous or something?

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:02.000
I see.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:05.290
I'm so hungry right now...

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:07.120
Oh! If that's the case!

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:14.910
Natsusa-<i>san </i>made these to hand out
after the match! I helped a bit, too.

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:17.660
A bit? You really only helped a bit?

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:19.450
Yes! Just a bit.

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:22.620
It's been a while since I ate
Natsusa's fermented brown rice!

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:23.950
No!

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:29.540
Ibuki-<i>senpai </i>was useless during the match
and Sei is being mean to me.

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:32.160
No way...

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.450
Natsusa-<i>san</i>!

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:36.080
Who is the one being mean here?

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:41.200
Here you go.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:43.660
H-He's so strong...

00:06:57.870 --> 00:06:59.200
Yasunari.

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:07.700
Don't make such an unhappy expression, Yasunari!

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:09.830
I'm not unhappy or anything.

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:14.080
Shingyouji-<i>san </i>showed me
a strange Buddhist website earlier.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:16.160
Is he all right?

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:17.450
Huh? So scary!

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:18.790
What'd he tell you?!

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:21.120
Something about his reason for being nervous...

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:22.580
Oh...

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:26.250
Yasunari, why do you play rugby?

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:29.410
I've never really thought about it.

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:34.700
I want to get good at rugby and
feel good winning matches, probably?

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:38.910
Right. Your goal is to win matches.

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:40.120
That's true...

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:42.250
I mean, is there any other reason?

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:45.790
That's what I think now, but that
wasn't the case for me in the past.

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:48.410
For Seiichirou, that has never been the goal.

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:54.910
Winning rugby matches isn't his goal,
it's just a method to achieve his goal.

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:58.000
I want him to sort himself out.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:01.040
So, Yasunari, I need your help.

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:02.410
Okay?

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:04.000
I reserved a two-person and three-person room.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:08.000
I'll take care of Seiichirou, so you two
take care of Natsusa for me.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.450
I understand.

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:11.080
Try your best.

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:14.160
It's about ten times more troublesome
than you probably think it is.

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:20.620
Hey, the fight between the two of you
is seriously annoying.

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:24.950
We aren't really fighting.
Natsu is just getting mad on his own.

00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:27.410
Just forget about it already.

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:31.120
You don't really mean that.

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:35.000
That's what Natsusa told you to say!

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:38.540
That scared me!

00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:40.700
Stop it! Seriously! That's not what I meant!

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:42.910
I really meant you should forget about it!

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:50.750
Come to think of it, Yasunari was worried
because you said weird things.

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:54.870
Yasunari gets nervous when
he thinks about winning.

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:58.200
But I have never thought about winning before.

00:08:58.200 --> 00:08:59.500
I know.

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:04.580
If that were the case, you wouldn't have
lost your touch at a time like this.

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:08.950
And you only get nervous
when Natsusa is around, right?

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:10.200
I believe so.

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:15.910
Before worrying about something like that,
do you know why you play rugby?

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:19.370
I ended up playing rugby because Natsu plays it.

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:22.330
In the past. But it's different now.

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:25.450
I mean, Natsusa doesn't play rugby anymore.

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:31.910
Tomorrow, we're going to Maisagi's rugby field.
Think it over while we're there.

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:37.620
Natsusa-<i>san</i>, would you like some tea?

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:39.580
I don't need any.

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:43.750
Even Yuu hates me. I can't go on anymore.

00:09:43.750 --> 00:09:46.370
I don't hate you! I love you!

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:50.660
Maybe it's better if I'm
not a manager, after all?

00:09:50.660 --> 00:09:54.410
No, I don't believe that's the case...

00:09:54.410 --> 00:09:58.950
Liar! I mean, you hated me
from the start, Yasunari!

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:00.950
You're bringing that up right now?!

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:02.120
You're wrong!

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:05.250
Yasunari-<i>kun </i>was mad at himself
because he couldn't catch up to you

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:07.620
and ended up lashing out at you!

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:09.080
It wasn't that he hated you!

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:10.370
In fact, he really likes you!

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:12.910
He analyzed me in such an
unpretentious manner! So scary!

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:14.250
That's not true!

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:17.200
Yasunari hates me, too!

00:10:21.910 --> 00:10:25.000
Yasunari-<i>kun</i>! You like Natsusa-<i>san</i>, don't you?

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:26.620
Y-Yeah...

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:29.450
Then say you like me to my face!

00:10:29.450 --> 00:10:31.200
That's right! Yasunari-<i>kun</i>!

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:34.080
Please properly tell Natsusa-<i>san</i>
that you like him!

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:37.540
He's a hundred times more
troublesome than I thought!

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:42.790
Morning.

00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:44.660
Good morning.

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:46.120
How was it?

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:48.000
It was absolute hell.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:49.700
I... I like you.

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:51.450
It doesn't feel like you do at all!

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:54.450
Tell him in a more serious manner!

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:57.370
Natsusa-<i>san </i>was probably doing it on purpose...

00:10:57.370 --> 00:10:58.660
Sounds like you had a rough time.

00:10:58.660 --> 00:11:00.620
So, what are we doing today?

00:11:00.620 --> 00:11:04.160
Hm? Well, let's get a rental car first.

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:06.040
Oh, but don't worry.

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:10.200
I'll take you to heaven as a reward
for working so hard yesterday.

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:16.910
Wow, they really got a new goal post!

00:11:16.910 --> 00:11:18.660
Too bad for us.

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:23.080
If they replaced it a little bit sooner,
we would have had a chance to use it.

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:25.500
So this is the field you all practiced on!

00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:28.000
Yeah! That's right!

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:30.200
Natsusa, want to stop by the club room?

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:32.040
Let's go!

00:11:35.080 --> 00:11:36.450
Huh?

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:44.040
This room is so nostalgic.

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:48.540
Come to think of it, this is where Madoka-<i>san</i>...

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:50.750
"Maisagi High School Rugby Team"

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:54.000
I fell for it!

00:12:00.290 --> 00:12:01.580
Did he notice?

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:02.750
Not when we left.

00:12:02.750 --> 00:12:04.040
Huh?

00:12:04.040 --> 00:12:05.370
See? He noticed.

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:06.660
Let's hurry and run!

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:08.410
Wh-What's going on?!

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:10.330
Where are Seiichirou-<i>san </i>and Natsusa-<i>san</i>?

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:12.450
They were annoying, so I left them behind.

00:12:12.450 --> 00:12:15.410
No way! This area doesn't have
a good transportation system!

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:19.540
That's why I did it. I want them both
to cool their heads a bit.

00:12:19.540 --> 00:12:21.080
But...

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:25.830
Yasunari, will you look at my smartphone?

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:33.000
"Natsusa Yuzuki"

00:12:33.410 --> 00:12:35.160
It's from Natsusa-<i>san</i>.

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:37.500
He bought these stamps, huh?

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:38.910
Should I reply?

00:12:38.910 --> 00:12:40.830
No, don't reply.

00:12:40.830 --> 00:12:43.200
He'll understand my message when
he sees I've read it, but ignored him.

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:45.790
I'm scared of what he'll do when he comes back.

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:47.910
Me, too.

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:52.000
But, well, the three of us should
kick back and do some sightseeing!

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:55.830
People never really explore the areas
they live, right? Where do you want to go?

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:59.950
Actually, I've never been to
any fizzy hot springs.

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:02.500
Is it Natsusa, again?

00:13:02.500 --> 00:13:02.910
"Sousuke Yamada"
Is it Natsusa, again?

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:05.660
"Sousuke Yamada"
No, it's from Yamada-<i>senpai</i>.

00:13:05.660 --> 00:13:08.000
"Sousuke Yamada"
Oh, let's ignore it. Decline him.

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:12.370
This time it's Syouta-<i>senpai</i>.

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:14.000
Decline.

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:15.700
It's Taylor-<i>senpai</i>.

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:17.330
Answer.

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:18.660
Don't call me!

00:13:18.660 --> 00:13:20.250
I'm back in Oita right now!

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:23.450
I don't have time to
deal with you guys right now!

00:13:23.450 --> 00:13:24.370
We know!

00:13:24.370 --> 00:13:25.950
That's why we're here?

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:28.950
Can you guess where we are right now?

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:30.330
Huh?

00:14:03.870 --> 00:14:06.290
What'd you come here for?

00:14:06.290 --> 00:14:09.950
Yesterday, I found out you were
going to Oita from Shingyouji.

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:12.910
That's why we thought we'd
take this chance to come, too.

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:15.450
That guy really can't read the room!

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:18.040
Oita is the best!

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:20.870
"Oita Station"
But what's here in Oita?

00:14:20.870 --> 00:14:22.200
No, I really can't.

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:25.410
I was going to have a relaxing
vacation day with my cute juniors

00:14:25.410 --> 00:14:30.540
and prepare myself for all the bullying
that Natsusa will start doing tomorrow.

00:14:30.540 --> 00:14:32.500
No, no. That's impossible.

00:14:32.500 --> 00:14:35.290
No, no, no. I can't do it. Seriously.

00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:37.450
Oh! Ibuki!

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:41.000
Oita is such a nice place.

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:43.500
Thanks for inviting us!

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:49.200
I had wanted to relax at the
hot springs before our big match!

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:51.410
Why are those two here?!

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:56.410
We knew that you wouldn't
show us around if it were only us!

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:00.660
Sousuke's turn! He summons
Captain and Vice-Captain!

00:15:00.660 --> 00:15:03.040
When the hell is it my turn?!

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:07.290
Ueoka, I want to try the chicken
tempura that's famous here.

00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:09.160
Do you know a good place?

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:11.450
I do!

00:15:14.080 --> 00:15:15.450
Taisei.

00:15:16.580 --> 00:15:18.290
Hey, Taisei.

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:21.620
Go home and get some rest.

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:23.870
Don't you have practice tomorrow?

00:15:26.160 --> 00:15:28.410
Jeez...

00:15:28.410 --> 00:15:30.660
Why is it always us?

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:37.540
Mako-<i>san </i>worked so hard and was the first
to enter Doushisha from our school...

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:40.620
We worked so hard to follow in his footsteps...

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:43.790
We didn't get in easily like Ueoka did!

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:46.290
And you worked so hard for this!

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:48.080
You're wrong, Taisei.

00:15:49.330 --> 00:15:52.660
It's not that people who work hard
get to play in matches.

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:58.040
Talented players who aren't hurt
are the ones who get to play. That's all.

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:05.540
Mako-<i>san </i>and I are working hard to accept it,
but you're getting in our way.

00:16:06.910 --> 00:16:11.330
Taisei, there is only one thing
we want from you.

00:16:11.330 --> 00:16:13.790
We want you to carry our school's name,

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:18.450
shine on the field, and win the nationals.

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:24.700
We don't want you to worry about us or
be hostile with the other team members.

00:16:30.040 --> 00:16:31.250
I'm going home.

00:16:31.250 --> 00:16:32.500
Yeah.

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:33.950
Hurry up and get better.

00:16:33.950 --> 00:16:35.200
Yeah.

00:16:37.580 --> 00:16:38.830
Taisei.

00:16:40.790 --> 00:16:43.540
But thank you.

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:44.950
Yeah.

00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:56.410
Ibuki-<i>senpai</i>! What's <i>yaseuma</i>?

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:57.830
Skinny horses?

00:16:57.830 --> 00:17:01.500
Ibuki-<i>senpai</i>! What's the difference between
chicken tempura and fried chicken?

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:04.750
Ibuki! This doesn't taste good at all. Why?

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:07.080
All of you shut up for a bit!

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:18.160
Is... Is there something on my face?

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:23.500
Nah. You prayed for a long time,
so I was wondering what you prayed for.

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:29.620
Huh? Oh! I was hoping that no one
would get hurt in the next match.

00:17:31.160 --> 00:17:32.290
That's so like you.

00:17:32.290 --> 00:17:36.450
Huh? Oh! Should I have wished for us to win?

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:38.450
Did I fail as a manager?

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:40.120
No. That's just who you are.

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:42.290
D-Do you mean that in a good way?

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:44.080
I do.

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:46.660
Thank goodness.

00:17:55.370 --> 00:17:59.370
Do you know why you play rugby?

00:17:59.370 --> 00:18:03.620
I ended up playing rugby
because Natsu asked me to play.

00:18:05.450 --> 00:18:08.750
Ever since I was little, there was
nothing I really wanted to do.

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:11.160
I just listened to Natsusa.

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:14.120
Hello!

00:18:14.120 --> 00:18:15.790
I'm Natsusa Yuzuki!

00:18:15.790 --> 00:18:17.080
What are you doing?

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:19.160
Nothing, really.

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:21.290
Then, let's play together over there!

00:18:21.290 --> 00:18:22.450
Let's go!

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:28.120
Sei-<i>chan</i>! Let's play hero!

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:32.620
Sei-<i>chan</i>! Let's split an ice cream bar!

00:18:32.620 --> 00:18:37.200
Sei-<i>chan</i>! Big brother Ibuki is going to
play in a match. Let's go watch!

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:44.120
Sei-<i>chan</i>, let's go to rugby school.

00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:49.000
You kick the ball into the goal
to get a conversion.

00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:51.370
I practiced so much every day.

00:18:51.370 --> 00:18:57.660
It should go in if I do it normally, so I don't
understand why everyone's missing.

00:18:57.660 --> 00:19:01.290
Even so, why did I start
missing all of a sudden?

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:04.200
What caused me to get nervous?

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:05.950
Sei...

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:13.750
Forget it...

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:16.410
I won't go anymore.

00:19:17.290 --> 00:19:21.660
If this'll be solved by not attending,
it'll be for the best.

00:19:23.290 --> 00:19:24.660
Natsu.

00:19:24.660 --> 00:19:25.950
Hm?

00:19:25.950 --> 00:19:30.870
The rehabilitation doctor
said you didn't go today.

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:36.040
I didn't see the point in getting
rehabilitation if I can't play rugby...

00:19:36.040 --> 00:19:39.580
What should I do when
I go back to the university?

00:19:39.580 --> 00:19:43.620
You'll probably be busy practicing rugby.

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:45.080
I'll quit rugby, too.

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:46.500
Huh?

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:50.500
I only played because you played.

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:52.540
I'll quit if you quit.

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:55.700
Y-You can't! You're so good!

00:19:55.700 --> 00:19:57.120
Not really.

00:19:57.120 --> 00:20:00.870
That's not true! I'll go
watch you practice every day!

00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:02.750
Of course, I'll go to all the matches.

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:04.160
Don't quit!

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:05.830
Please!

00:20:08.540 --> 00:20:12.290
Got it. But don't come to practice every day.

00:20:12.290 --> 00:20:13.910
It'll be bad for you in the winter.

00:20:13.910 --> 00:20:15.790
I want to go.

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:16.790
No.

00:20:16.790 --> 00:20:19.830
What? Well, but thank goodness.

00:20:19.830 --> 00:20:23.580
I was so surprised! I didn't think
you'd say something like that.

00:20:24.620 --> 00:20:26.330
It's been a while.

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:27.540
Huh?

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:32.000
You hadn't smiled since the accident.

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:34.120
R-Really?

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:37.580
I love watching you play rugby, Sei!

00:20:37.580 --> 00:20:39.040
Especially your conversion kicks!

00:20:39.040 --> 00:20:41.910
Even though I know you'll score,
it makes my heart race

00:20:41.910 --> 00:20:44.950
and it feels so good when you make it.

00:20:44.950 --> 00:20:48.750
It makes me happy and
I can't get that feeling often!

00:20:50.120 --> 00:20:54.410
Then, what'll happen if I don't make it?

00:20:54.410 --> 00:20:57.500
Will he stop smiling again?

00:20:58.540 --> 00:21:00.910
It was like I started getting eaten away

00:21:00.910 --> 00:21:04.790
the moment that thought came to mind.
The stability in my kicks faded...

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:08.330
...and I stopped being able to make the kicks.

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:15.200
Don't make that kind of face.

00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:17.330
I don't want you to make that kind of face.

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:20.700
Sei? Ouch! Ouch! Ouch! What is it?!

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:22.200
Smile.

00:21:22.200 --> 00:21:23.410
Huh?

00:21:23.410 --> 00:21:24.450
Hurry.

00:21:24.450 --> 00:21:27.250
Uh? L-Like this?

00:21:27.250 --> 00:21:28.370
Smile more naturally.

00:21:28.370 --> 00:21:30.950
Are you giving me acting advice?!

00:21:36.160 --> 00:21:39.830
Natsu, you love watching me play, right?

00:21:39.830 --> 00:21:40.910
Yeah.

00:21:40.910 --> 00:21:42.160
Even now?

00:21:42.160 --> 00:21:43.000
Huh?

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:47.120
Even though I can't make the conversion kicks?

00:21:47.120 --> 00:21:48.450
Do you still like watching me?

00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:52.250
O-Of course I still like watching you.

00:21:52.250 --> 00:21:53.950
I love it!

00:21:55.200 --> 00:21:56.830
I see.

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:03.870
If Natsu will smile whether
the ball goes in or not...

00:22:03.870 --> 00:22:05.540
There's nothing to be nervous about.

00:22:16.750 --> 00:22:18.910
Huh? Oh... You did it!

00:22:18.910 --> 00:22:20.040
You did it! You did it!

00:22:20.040 --> 00:22:22.370
It went in! You did it!

00:22:22.370 --> 00:22:24.830
You should do it again
before you forget the feeling!

00:22:24.830 --> 00:22:27.450
No, I'm fine now.

00:22:28.410 --> 00:22:32.540
I know that I've already gotten what I wanted.

00:22:38.040 --> 00:22:40.330
Huh? Did you forget something, Taisei?

00:22:40.330 --> 00:22:41.160
You must be tired.

00:22:41.160 --> 00:22:44.000
Oh, hello.

00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:46.040
Taisei finally went home?

00:22:46.040 --> 00:22:49.410
Huh? Were you waiting until he left?

00:22:49.410 --> 00:22:52.450
It's hard to face him right now.

00:22:52.450 --> 00:22:55.540
I'm sorry. You should have contacted me.

00:22:55.540 --> 00:22:59.830
No, it's fine. When did
they say you'll get better?

00:22:59.830 --> 00:23:05.410
They said it'll be about three months
before I can play rugby again.

00:23:05.410 --> 00:23:06.830
I see.

00:23:08.040 --> 00:23:10.620
Oh! Do you want something to drink?

00:23:10.620 --> 00:23:12.290
Taisei brought me something over there...

00:23:12.290 --> 00:23:13.910
It's frustrating.

00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:19.540
It must be frustrating, Taku.

00:23:22.410 --> 00:23:28.370
It is... I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

00:23:28.370 --> 00:23:29.830
Something like this...

00:23:30.950 --> 00:23:34.080
Me, too. I'm sorry...

00:23:41.580 --> 00:23:44.450
Of course it's really frustrating...

00:23:44.450 --> 00:23:46.910
"Carbonic acid hot springs aren't too hot,
so you can stay in them a long time."
